&lt;p&gt;Salem, OR &ndash; The Oregon Housing Needs Analysis (OHNA) is part of Oregon&rsquo;s statewide land use planning system that is intended to facilitate housing production, affordability and choice to meet housing needs for Oregonians statewide, outlined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Folis.oregonlegislature.gov%2Fliz%2F2023R1%2FDownloads%2FMeasureDocument%2FHB2001&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Candrea.chiapella%40das.oregon.gov%7Cb5d17b33f2384bfcd3d608dd365befc4%7Caa3f6932fa7c47b4a0cea598cad161cf%7C0%7C0%7C638726490671971153%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=E%2FoIlB9UE%2FJFT8EoWOZAotUbssS62hSySYKydQYcgBY%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0"&gt;House Bill 2001&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Oregon Department of Administrative Services published the Office of Economic Analysis&rsquo; &lt;a href="https://www.oregon.gov/das/oea/Documents/OHNA-2026-Results-Report.pdf"&gt;2026 Production Targets and Adopted Methodology&lt;/a&gt;. The report presents both the final methodology and the initial statewide and regional results. The OHNA report will be updated and released annually by Dec. 31.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For more information on OHNA, visit the &lt;a href="https://www.oregon.gov/das/oea/Pages/Oregon-Housing-Needs-Analysis-Methodology.aspx"&gt;Office of Economic Analysis webpage&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lane County, Ore. (Jan. 15, 2026)-&lt;/strong&gt; On Monday, January 12, 2026, at 8:57 a.m., Oregon State Police responded to a single vehicle crash on Highway 58, near milepost 40, in Lane County.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The preliminary investigation indicated an eastbound Ford F-250, operated by Aaron Henry Longton (64) of Port Orford, lost control and rolled in the ditch. The roll event ejected the operator and sole occupant of the vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The operator of the Ford (Longton) was declared deceased after being transported to an area hospital.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The highway was not impacted during the on-scene investigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OSP was assisted by Oakridge Fire and ODOT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;# # #&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;
The Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU) is a specialized unit responsible for investigating fatal and critical injury collisions on Oregon&rsquo;s highways. The team provides expertise in the documentation, investigation, and analysis of complex motor vehicle crashes and crime scenes. They receive specialized training in the use of advanced measuring techniques and small unmanned aircraft systems (sUAS) for on-scene investigations. The CRU team includes ACTAR accredited collision reconstructionists and technical collision investigators deployed across the state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yamhill County, Ore. (Jan. 15, 2026)-&lt;/strong&gt; On Tuesday, January 13, 2026, at 8:43 a.m., Oregon State Police responded to a two-vehicle crash on Highway 154, near milepost 6, in Yamhill County.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The preliminary investigation indicated a southbound Kia Spectra, operated by Marcel Israel Benavides (35) of Dayton, crossed the centerline for unknown reasons and struck a northbound International commercial motor vehicle and trailer, operated by Jose Armando Perez Torres (26) of Salem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The operator of the Kia (Benavides) was declared deceased at the scene.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The operator of the International (Perez Torres) was reportedly uninjured.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The highway was impacted for approximately four hours during the on-scene investigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;OSP was assisted by the Yamhill County Sheriff's Office, Dayton Fire and Rescue, Lafayette Fire and Rescue, McMinnville Fire District, and ODOT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;# # #&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;
The Oregon State Police Collision Reconstruction Unit (CRU) is a specialized unit responsible for investigating fatal and critical injury collisions on Oregon&rsquo;s highways. The team provides expertise in the documentation, investigation, and analysis of complex motor vehicle crashes and crime scenes. They receive specialized training in the use of advanced measuring techniques and small unmanned aircraft systems (sUAS) for on-scene investigations. The CRU team includes ACTAR accredited collision reconstructionists and technical collision investigators deployed across the state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Lane County Clerk&rsquo;s Office will help couples tie the knot or renew their vows on Valentine&rsquo;s Day this year.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&ldquo;What better day to marry your sweetheart than on Valentine&rsquo;s Day?&rdquo; said Lane County Clerk Tommy Gong. &ldquo;All of us at the Clerk&rsquo;s Office are excited to be able to offer couples the opportunity to schedule marriage ceremonies on the holiday this year.&rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are 32 slots available to schedule on a first come, first served basis. Ceremonies will be conducted in 30-minute intervals from 10:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m. on Saturday, February 14, at the County Clerk&rsquo;s Office at 125 E. 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; Avenue, Eugene.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four Clerk&rsquo;s Office employees will officiate the marriages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To schedule a ceremony, couples must first obtain a valid marriage license from the Clerk&rsquo;s Office (125 E. 8&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt;&amp;nbsp;Avenue, Eugene). To obtain a marriage license, couples fill out the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapps.lanecounty.org%2FMarriage%2FDateSelect%3F_gl%3D1*1i0komt*_ga*MTU3MTk4NTc0LjE3NDcyMzQ5MTY.*_ga_G30BCGQ9RY*czE3NTYyNTMxOTQkbzY2JGcxJHQxNzU2MjUzMjQ5JGo1JGwwJGgw&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cpublicinformation%40lanecountyor.gov%7C0c5953b0045f4fdab47e08ddebc5afb5%7C74df5a22826e49429a741d199974dedf%7C0%7C0%7C638925956491706082%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=9scRbWJF%2FwCIfr%2BBQaVOu8f2h%2BR9gotoCtpM5uhELOw%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0"&gt;online Marriage License Application&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and then must visit the Clerk&rsquo;s Office at least three days before the ceremony to complete the license process. Couples already married may consider renewing their vows on Valentine&rsquo;s Day too; no new marriage license required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The marriage license fee is $60 and a marriage officiated by the County Clerk is $117. Additional details, including license requirements and scheduling information, can be found on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lanecounty.org%2Fcms%2FOne.aspx%3FportalId%3D3585881%26pageId%3D4081150&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cpublicinformation%40lanecountyor.gov%7C0c5953b0045f4fdab47e08ddebc5afb5%7C74df5a22826e49429a741d199974dedf%7C0%7C0%7C638925956491722719%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=FT%2FqzIkG7dKP3P3%2BydchEIXZtRNimaBvDL7FKcwyI84%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0"&gt;the Lane County Clerk&rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

